      "cooked": "<p>I know the rule book states that cards act in the orer they entered the field, but I still have some questions.&nbsp;</p><p>Let's say we're playing in the sewers.</p><p>I'm playing Ra, you are playing AZ. You bring out your Focused Apertures in round one. On round two I bring out Imbued Fire. Now all damage is fire damage. But your card was in play first, so do you add your +1 from the Apertures before applying the effect of my card?&nbsp;</p><p>Now let's say Irradiated Cyclohexane Vat comes out. Do we add our +1s to damage because our cards were out first?&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:07.187Z",
