      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-02T14:58:26.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Lowendz113\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lowendz113/48/2068_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Lowendz113:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I know the rule book states that cards act in the orer they entered the field, but I still have some questions.&nbsp;Let's say we're playing in the sewers.I'm playing Ra, you are playing AZ. You bring out your Focused Apertures in round one. On round two I bring out Imbued Fire. Now all damage is fire damage. But your card was in play first, so do you add your +1 from the Apertures before applying the effect of my card?&nbsp;Now let's say Irradiated Cyclohexane Vat comes out. Do we add our +1s to damage because our cards were out first?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This has been discussed extensively. My apologies for not having a handy reference.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The rule of thumb I developed for myself based on the discussion is that one determines the type of the attack before applying any increases or reductions.</p>",
